# A CANDIDATE: THE LIVE ENGINE b190673dbdbf AND TWO FIXES ITS CARD ROWS LED TO
# (2026-11-25).
#   SERIES_FILE=deploy/localai/patches/staged/engine-refusal.series \
#     sh deploy/localai/llama-cpp/build.sh sycl_f16 <out dir>      # the live INTEL_STACK
# engine-next.series, line for line, then:
#   0018  the pool's refusal is not a std::exception: it reaches the graph.
#         Staged 0013 said "a refused pool commit fails the request" and did
#         not: with 0016's switch the backend process ended at its first
#         refusal (docs/notes/room-on-the-card.md §4). The op that asks for
#         the memory catches every std::exception and aborts.
#   0020  the speech port keeps nothing of a saved voice in memory between
#         requests: its rows are read from the profile's own file each time,
#         its samples and rows zeroed. The live engine kept the last clip's
#         samples for as long as it stayed loaded - a deleted voice outliving
#         its delete (docs/notes/omnivoice-on-our-backend.md §13).
# (0019 is a patch of LocalAI's SERVER and is in no engine series.)
# With every switch off it must gate as b190673dbdbf does, fingerprint for
# fingerprint, or it rolls back. Its own rows: a reranker copy with
# GGML_SYCL_POOL_REFUSE=2 against a control — the first two requests that
# grow the pool answered with an error by the SAME process, the third served
# with the control's scores; and the port — every sentence in a profile's
# voice after the first says "read from its kept encoding", none "kept".
# THE PORT BECOMES THE LIVE VOICE ONLY ON THIS ENGINE (the architecture
# session, 2026-11-25): b190673dbdbf never serves a voice through it.
